                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bd370aec-0b02-3923-b7ec-f5ee3bf108f3",
                        "entry_id": "a8459703-70c5-3358-8179-0abd6d6b74fe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ijsje"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4f24ff6-25f6-47d4-b02f-959c2ee4f029",
                                "sense_id": "bd370aec-0b02-3923-b7ec-f5ee3bf108f3",
                                "text": "Ik breng mijn weekend door met jou in Scheveningen.\nDe zee is lauw, de lucht is blauw in Scheveningen.\nDaar kan je braaien in het zand,\nMet een ijsco in je hand,\nZo samen aan het stille strand in Scheveningen.\nLouis Davids"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fcccf45c-0e5e-4c3f-a5b0-36e5101f988c",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8459703-70c5-3358-8179-0abd6d6b74fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "bd370aec-0b02-3923-b7ec-f5ee3bf108f3",
                        "target_lang_word": "ice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "665a7fd0-00fd-3703-9874-27ecf2d15898",
                                        "entry_id": "2b600705-5a46-39cc-b6dc-77733c1e9e7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Water in frozen (solid) form."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef599715-fa28-4db1-9dee-4122205f38ce",
                                                "sense_id": "665a7fd0-00fd-3703-9874-27ecf2d15898",
                                                "text": "If thou doſt marry, Ile giue thee / This plague to thy dowry: / Be thou as chaſte as yce, as pure as ſnowe, / Thou ſhalt not ſcape calumny, to a Nunnery goe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "acd1e30e-7ea7-46c6-81f9-1dc90383d45e",
                                                "sense_id": "665a7fd0-00fd-3703-9874-27ecf2d15898",
                                                "text": "1882, Popular Science Monthly (volume 20), \"The Freezing of a Salt Lake\"\nIt has always been difficult to explain how ice is formed on the surface of oceans while the temperature of maximum density is lower than that of cogelation, and the observations on this lake were instituted in the hope that they might throw light upon the subject."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b919ec6-9334-49ae-9146-67407b51ee5b",
                                                "sense_id": "665a7fd0-00fd-3703-9874-27ecf2d15898",
                                                "text": "Of all the transitions brought about on the Earth’s surface by temperature change, the melting of ice into water is the starkest. It is binary. And for the land beneath, the air above and the life around, it changes everything."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "501d96de-8030-3668-9e40-2129ed3889c8",
                                        "entry_id": "2b600705-5a46-39cc-b6dc-77733c1e9e7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any frozen volatile chemical, such as ammonia or carbon dioxide."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f524bbfb-46af-37ec-b272-5ca0148731e3",
                                        "entry_id": "2b600705-5a46-39cc-b6dc-77733c1e9e7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any volatile chemical, such as water, ammonia, or carbon dioxide, not necessarily in solid form, when discussing the composition of e.g. a planet as an ice giant vs a gas giant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbf092ec-50d8-47eb-acc6-f3253ee35fbb",
                                                "sense_id": "f524bbfb-46af-37ec-b272-5ca0148731e3",
                                                "text": "Above the core is the lower-density liquid mantle composed of ice materials under high pressure and temperature. This massive liquid layer would not be separated into layers of traditional ice compounds, but mixtures of radically different compounds originally consisting of water, carbon dioxide, methane, and ammonia […] Since the mass of the planet is dominated by the liquid mantle that itself consists of heated ices under pressure, both Uranus and Neptune are classified as giant ice planets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c15f6c4a-8d52-44aa-8e95-f58685d2928a",
                                                "sense_id": "f524bbfb-46af-37ec-b272-5ca0148731e3",
                                                "text": "Uranus and Neptune are […] usually classified separately as ice giants because they contain a much higher proportion of ice-forming substances such as water, ammonia, and methane. […] In the case of Uranus, the ice mantle must make up between 9.3 and 13.4 Earth masses worth of the total mass of the planet, which is 14.5 Earth masses. Similar proportions apply to Neptune. The commonly used term \"ice mantle\" is someone misleading, since the substance is actually a hot, slushy mixture that would be more aptly described as a water–ammonia ocean."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd94c7fd-66bd-4069-b63b-727c00123d9c",
                                                "sense_id": "f524bbfb-46af-37ec-b272-5ca0148731e3",
                                                "text": "Neptune has one major moon: Triton, which is comparable in size to the Jovian moon Europa and at an average density of 2.061 g/cm³ widely understood to be covered by several hundred km of frozen or liquid ice."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "916d0791-2d4d-343c-990f-0059ff28bb4d",
                                        "entry_id": "2b600705-5a46-39cc-b6dc-77733c1e9e7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something having an extreme coldness of manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19b9c886-8614-43d0-81f3-ccc149fe435d",
                                                "sense_id": "916d0791-2d4d-343c-990f-0059ff28bb4d",
                                                "text": "a heart of ice"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e82bb42-e976-48e8-aaca-93ebac1b36e5",
                                                "sense_id": "916d0791-2d4d-343c-990f-0059ff28bb4d",
                                                "text": "Her eyes flash with anger, her voice ice. \"You afraid of the law? You haven't changed. I want you out of my house now.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65d1155f-765a-341c-a766-dbcbe4f90d95",
                                        "entry_id": "2b600705-5a46-39cc-b6dc-77733c1e9e7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something, such as awkwardness, that prevents open social interaction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ebfc255-9c41-4cae-b4f1-be1231878437",
                                                "sense_id": "65d1155f-765a-341c-a766-dbcbe4f90d95",
                                                "text": "The dialogues—or \"raps\"—usually take place on a monthly or bi-monthly basis and aim at fostering contacts hand at breaking through stereotypical notions held by both sides. \"There's no question that there's ice to begin with,\" said Lance Bradley, who conducts the raps for Chelsea's Tenth Precinct."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fb8160f-e7ef-45e4-887c-4115af5fd24f",
                                                "sense_id": "65d1155f-765a-341c-a766-dbcbe4f90d95",
                                                "text": "break the ice"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e876e33-938d-30e0-899a-f2fd3d192bbe",
                                        "entry_id": "2b600705-5a46-39cc-b6dc-77733c1e9e7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The area where a game of ice hockey is played."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee4aa3ff-bdf0-45cf-b111-1e2fd0e5c65d",
                                                "sense_id": "9e876e33-938d-30e0-899a-f2fd3d192bbe",
                                                "text": "2006, CBC, Finland, Sweden 'the dream final', February 26 2002,\nThe neighbouring countries have enjoyed many great battles on the ice. They last met for gold at the 1998 world championship, won by Sweden. Three years earlier, Finland bested Sweden for the only world title in its history."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45bc71e1-65f3-3c93-b118-3f55c0c82dfb",
                                        "entry_id": "2b600705-5a46-39cc-b6dc-77733c1e9e7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Icing; frosting (\\\"a sweet, often creamy and thick glaze made primarily of sugar\\\")."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dialectal",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b92de83-0344-4c46-9d47-9a4951897108",
                                                "sense_id": "45bc71e1-65f3-3c93-b118-3f55c0c82dfb",
                                                "text": "Well weddings, they were just the usual ... my big brother was married in the Masonic and the Co-operative done the party. Steak pie and tatties, and all that sort of stuff. The wee square Albert cake with ice on it, fruit cake. Then the wee dance after that. There was no drinking at oor wedding!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0ef89027-793e-39c4-a02f-acb2a0257e78",
                                        "entry_id": "2b600705-5a46-39cc-b6dc-77733c1e9e7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A frozen dessert made of fruit juice, water and sugar."
                                        ],
